 we're pretty excited about the  usefulness that we think this is going  to provide  as a final example which is shown  conceptually here  is a dual reporter assay that we think  would be really relevant in pharmacology  and drug discovery  with the dual reporter system you could  simultaneously measure  a free versus a bound drug if you have  specific antibodies  that recognize the free form of the drug  and the bound form of the drug  you could label them with different  reporters and measure them  simultaneously  although not drawn here you might  envision that the antibody specific for  the free drug would actually bind to  both forms  depending on the location of the epitope  but then you would be able to measure  the bound  form as a percentage of the total that  was present in the sample  so we think this is a really kind of  creative  and interesting possible application  for the dual reporter system and we're  really excited to see somebody  try it out and let us know how it works  so now before we finish up  i would like to pass the presentation  back over to josh for some closing  remarks  thank you so the next slide  is where i want to circle back to talk a  little bit more about uh when sherry  was discussing the ada and isotyping in  the in the same well  uh currently this is not being done at  least as far as i know  by any other technology so either you do  just the ada or then you do the  isotaping isotype them separately  and then you're either typing each one  separately so that could be multiple  eliza's  um or multiple other types of of acid  that you're doing  with this study that was done you can  now  combine both the ada and the isotoping  into a single well which  obviously is going to reduce workflow  reduce sample needed  and reduce time to answers so uh  luminex is launching what we're calling  the xmap ada  study starter pack where we provide the  beads coupling kits and  all the ancillary agents that are needed  to complete the  to build the assay while these assays  are custom  because each capture molecule is going  to be different  the great thing is we have both field  application scientists  that are available to assist in  developing these types of assets for you  and then we also have  um our custom asset development lab  based in austin called the explore lab  so we really like this this is going to  you know this offering is going to  allow for you to get your answers in a  much faster  and more cost effective manner so if you  have any questions about that  please feel free to reach out to me or  to share  so that's our last slide this one ended  with a thank you  thank you sherry for that presentation  very informative  um as i said before we're very excited  about the intelliflex you can see  the applications that we've already  shown that that are  that are available on the new instrument  and then  also some applications that are  conceptually  relevant and we feel like you know this  is really going to  assist in your drug development moving  forward so thanks again  and we look forward to fielding any  questions that you may have
 

